<p>Rock salt is the cheapest and works down to roughly 15&ndash;20&deg;F. Calcium
chloride keeps working far colder and acts fastest. Magnesium chloride and CMA
are the gentler options, and are what most products labelled pet-safe are built
from. For most Yonkers driveways the honest answer is that the cheapest product
that works at tonight's temperature, spread thinly and shovelled promptly, does
less damage than anything applied heavily.</p>

